      "claim": "Chrysin, a structurally related polyphenolic flavone with multiple phenolic hydroxyls, has measured human oral bioavailability of only 0.003–0.02%, supporting low F for the query's phenolic heteroaromatic acid scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C13"],
      "claim": "Baicalein, another polyhydroxylated flavonoid, is clinically limited by low oral bioavailability, indicating that multiple phenolic groups and poor metabolic stability can drive F below 20%.",
